  "worked_solution": "First, we pull out the factor of $4$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{9x-2}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{9x-2}{4(x+1/4)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{9x-2}{(x+1/4)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{4}$ | $9$ | $-2$ |\n|  | $\u2193$ | $-\\frac{9}{4}$ |\n|  | $9$ | $-\\frac{17}{4}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9x-2}{(x+1/4)} & =9-\\frac{(17/4)}{(x+1/4)} \\\\  & =9-\\frac{17}{4x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{9x-2}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(9-\\frac{17}{4x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[9{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x-17{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[9x-\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|4x+1|]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[9(1-0)-\\frac{17}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|5|-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[9-\\frac{17\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}{4}] \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}-\\frac{17}{16}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(5).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
